{% comment %}
  RYOP — Phase 1: canonicalise collection tag-filter URLs to the parent collection.

  PROBLEM THIS FIXES
  Six tag-filter URLs under /collections/custom-rolling-papers each duplicate
  2,534–2,741 words of the parent page's 2,699 words:
      /collections/custom-rolling-papers/LOW-MOQ
      /collections/custom-rolling-papers/Custom-Gift-Sets
      /collections/custom-rolling-papers/Custom-Printed-Rolling-Papers
      /collections/custom-rolling-papers/samples
      /collections/custom-rolling-papers/booklets
      /collections/custom-rolling-papers/booklets-with-tips
  Several also exist in BOTH capitalised and lowercase form, doubling the count.
  The /samples variant still holds 7 organic positions, so these are being
  indexed in practice regardless of the noindex tag already in place.

  Tag URLs cannot be 301-redirected in Shopify — they are generated on the fly.
  The correct fix is a canonical pointing at the parent collection, which
  consolidates the signal instead of just hiding the page.

  HOW TO APPLY
  In layout/theme.liquid, find the existing canonical line — it will look like:

      <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">

  Replace that ONE line with the block below. Keep the existing
  noindex snippet (current_tags / current_page) exactly as it is; canonical and
  noindex do different jobs and both should stay.

  WHY BOTH: noindex keeps the tag URL out of the index; the canonical tells
  Google which URL the content and its link equity actually belong to.
{% endcomment %}

{%- if collection and current_tags -%}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}">
{%- elsif collection and current_page > 1 -%}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ shop.url }}{{ collection.url }}">
{%- else -%}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
{%- endif -%}
